<custom>
Via MEL system: Use MEL Query form to identify dataset.
Use order form to request data.
A MEL subset description follows:
&lt;MEL&gt;
&lt;PROLOGUE&gt;
ORDER_EMAIL = mel@eifel.nrlmry.navy.mil
&lt;/PROLOGUE&gt;

&lt;DATASET NAME = GOES_9_CONUS&gt;

DELIV_FMT = HDF

&lt;LOCAL&gt;
Satellite_Name: GOES_9
Sensor_Name: GOES_IMAGER
Database: NEONS_IMAGE
Geog_Location: Continental United States
&lt;/LOCAL&gt;

&lt;ACTION NAME = SUBSET&gt;

&lt;DIMENSION NAME = CHANNEL_NUMBER&gt;
UNITS = NULL
CHOICE_TYPE = MULTIPLE
#VALUES = 0.63 micro m VIS, 6.7 micro m VAP, 10.8 micro m IR
VALUES = 1, 3, 4
DEFAULTS = 1
&lt;/DIMENSION&gt;

&lt;DIMENSION NAME = TIME&gt;
UNITS = YYYYMMDDhh.hh
CHOICE_TYPE = RANGE
&lt;/DIMENSION&gt;

&lt;DIMENSION NAME = LONGITUDE&gt;
UNITS = deg.dd  #  decimal degrees + is E - is W
CHOICE_TYPE = RANGE
&lt;/DIMENSION&gt;

&lt;DIMENSION NAME = LATITUDE&gt;
UNITS = deg.dd  #  decimal degrees + is N - is S
CHOICE_TYPE = RANGE
&lt;/DIMENSION&gt;

&lt;/ACTION&gt;  #  end of subsetting
&lt;/DATASET&gt;
&lt;/MEL&gt;  #  end of the message
</custom>
<techpreq>MEL requires an HTML Browser (e.g. Mosaic), an Internet connection, email, and a use delivery site (email or anonymous ftp).</techpreq>
